Day 09 of my bug bounty series: understanding input validation.

Many vulnerabilities come down to one thing: an app trusted input it shouldn't have.

Today I learned 4 things:

1. User input: why every piece of user data must be validated.
2. Client vs server: browser-side checks can be bypassed, so the server must check too.
3. Encoding: URL, HTML and Base64 basics.
4. Common mistakes: input handling issues that can turn into vulnerabilities.

Never trust the browser. That's the lesson of the day.

